{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"partition","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"by","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"belongsInSecondPartition"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:SM7ElementQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/MutableCollection\/Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/MutableCollection\/Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:SM5IndexQa"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"belongsInSecondPartition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A predicate used to partition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the collection. All elements satisfying this predicate are ordered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after all elements not satisfying it."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The index of the first element in the reordered collection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that matches ","type":"text"},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If no elements in the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection match "},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the returned index is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equal to the collection’s "},{"code":"endIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After partitioning a collection, there is a pivot index "},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"no element before ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" satisfies the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"belongsInSecondPartition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"predicate and every element at or after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":" satisfies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"belongsInSecondPartition","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This operation isn’t guaranteed to be","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"stable, so the relative ordering of elements within the partitions might","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In the following example, an array of numbers is partitioned by a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"predicate that matches elements greater than 30.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var numbers = [30, 40, 20, 30, 30, 60, 10]","let p = numbers.partition(by: { $0 > 30 })","\/\/ p == 5","\/\/ numbers == [30, 10, 20, 30, 30, 60, 40]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"numbers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" array is now arranged in two partitions. The first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"partition, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"numbers[..<p]"},{"type":"text","text":", is made up of the elements that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are not greater than 30. The second partition, "},{"code":"numbers[p...]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is made up of the elements that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"are"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" greater than 30."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let first = numbers[..<p]","\/\/ first == [30, 10, 20, 30, 30]","let second = numbers[p...]","\/\/ second == [60, 40]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note that the order of elements in both partitions changed."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"That is, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"40"},{"type":"text","text":" appears before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"60"},{"type":"text","text":" in the original collection,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but, after calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"partition(by:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"60"},{"type":"text","text":" appears before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"40"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" is the length of the collection."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity","style":"note"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/dictionary\/values-swift.struct\/partition(by:)"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Standard Library"}],"role":"symbol","platforms":[{"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"8.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false},{"introducedAt":"13.0","beta":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst",